@event lyra_between_drills
# en: Again
title [fb56ef] = 再来
# en: {~{o} asked Lyra to help {o.them} with {o.their} duelling. Lyra said yes. That was a week ago. {o} now flinches at the word "again".|{o} limps into supper with singed cuffs and the look of someone who has been told "again" two hundred times.|You find {o} asleep on the library steps, wand still in hand. "Lyra," {o} says, without opening {o.their} eyes, as if that explains it.} "She won't stop," {o} tells you. "And I can't ask her to. You know what she's like."
text [87210a] = {~{o}请莱拉帮{o.them}练决斗。莱拉答应了。那是一个星期前的事。如今{o}一听到“再来”两个字就发抖。|{o}一瘸一拐地来吃晚饭，袖口烧焦了，一副被说了两百遍“再来”的样子。|你发现{o}在图书馆台阶上睡着了，手里还握着魔杖。“莱拉，”{o}眼睛都没睁就说，好像这就解释了一切。}“她不肯停，”{o}对你说，“我又没法开口求她。你知道她是什么样的人。”
# en: An empty duelling floor at dusk, one student lying flat on their back, another standing over them with a wand, saying something short.
scene [505963] = 黄昏时空荡的决斗场上，一个学生仰面躺倒，另一个拿着魔杖站在旁边，简短地说了句什么。
# en: Talk to Lyra
opt.left.label [1dfb56] = 去跟莱拉谈谈
# en: {~"Too hard?" Lyra looks genuinely baffled. "I'm not being hard. I'm being thorough." The next morning there's a flask of tea by the duelling ring, and nobody says who brought it.|Lyra listens with her arms folded. "Fine," she says. That afternoon she lets {o} rest for a full minute, and then, without being asked, shows {o.them} how to fall.|"{o} said that?" Lyra is silent for a while. "{o} should have said so." She doesn't apologise. She does turn up with new cuffs.}
opt.left.say.1 [1d36a3] = {~“太狠了？”莱拉一脸真心的困惑。“我不是狠。我是严谨。”第二天早上，决斗场边多了一壶茶，没人说是谁带来的。|莱拉抱着胳膊听你说完。“行，”她说。那天下午，她让{o}整整休息了一分钟，然后没人要求，就教了{o.them}怎么摔倒。|“{o}这么说的？”莱拉沉默了一会儿。“{o}应该直说。”她没有道歉。但她带来了新袖口。}
# en: {~"If {o} wanted it gentle, {o} should have asked someone gentle." Lyra turns back to the ring. "Again."|Lyra hears you out and says, "No." Then, after a moment: "Tell {o} the footwork is improving." You're not sure that helps.|"Do I tell you how to study?" says Lyra, who tells you how to study weekly. The drills continue.}
opt.left.say.2 [915b14] = {~“{o}要是想要温柔的，{o}就该去找温柔的人。”莱拉转回场上。“再来。”|莱拉听完说：“不。”过了一会儿又说：“告诉{o}，步法有进步。”你不确定这算不算帮上忙。|“我教过你怎么学习吗？”每周都在教你怎么学习的莱拉说。训练照旧。}
# en: Tell {o} to stick with it
opt.right.label [153231] = 劝{o}坚持下去
# en: {~{o} sticks with it. A month later {o} disarms a third-year in practice and looks so astonished that Lyra almost smiles.|{o} groans, and goes back. Lyra doesn't say "well done". She says "acceptable", which, you explain to {o}, is the same thing.|{o} goes back to the ring with the face of someone going to the gallows. It does get easier. It never gets easy.}
opt.right.say.1 [e1b469] = {~{o}坚持了下来。一个月后，{o}在练习中缴了一个三年级生的械，惊讶得连莱拉都差点笑了。|{o}哀叹一声，回去了。莱拉没说“干得好”。她说“还行”——你向{o}解释，这是同一个意思。|{o}一脸上刑场的表情回到场上。确实变得容易了些。但从来没变得容易。}

@event lyra_between_furniture
# en: You Sit Next to Her
title [ea12e1] = 你就坐她旁边
# en: {o} has sat next to Lyra in lectures since the first week. Today Lyra turns to you, across {o}, and asks, "Who is this?" {o} is right there. {o} has lent her ink. Twice.
text [d109e2] = 从第一周起，{o}上课就坐在莱拉旁边。今天，莱拉隔着{o}转过头问你：“这是谁？”{o}就在那儿。{o}借过她墨水。两次。
# en: A lecture bench, a proud student looking straight ahead, the classmate beside her waving a hand slowly in front of her face.
scene [1488dc] = 讲堂的长凳上，一个骄傲的学生目视前方，旁边的同学正慢慢在她眼前挥手。
# en: Introduce them properly
opt.left.label [bcff05] = 好好介绍他们认识
# en: "This is {o}, who sits next to you, and lends you ink." Lyra looks at {o} as if {o} had just appeared out of the air, then nods, very formally. The next morning, there's a new bottle of ink on {o}'s desk. Expensive ink.
opt.left.say.1 [7d5caa] = “这是{o}，坐你旁边，借你墨水的人。”莱拉看着{o}，像是{o}刚从空气里冒出来，然后郑重地点了点头。第二天早上，{o}桌上多了一瓶新墨水。很贵的墨水。
# en: Laugh it off
opt.right.label [29c02a] = 笑着带过
# en: You laugh, and Lyra doesn't see the joke, and {o} laughs too, a beat late. {o} moves two seats along the next week. Lyra doesn't notice that either.
opt.right.say.1 [9ab81e] = 你笑了，莱拉没明白笑点，{o}也跟着笑了，慢了半拍。下个星期，{o}挪远了两个座位。莱拉同样没注意到。

@event lyra_between_beaten
# en: How Did They Do It
title [5af8bc] = 怎么做到的
# en: {o} beat Lyra in practice today. Only a practice bout, only a point, and the whole hall saw. Lyra finds you afterwards. She doesn't say please; she has never said please first. "You were watching. How did {o} do it?"
text [57a714] = {o}今天在练习中赢了莱拉。只是一场练习赛，只差一分，可全场都看见了。莱拉事后找到你。她没说“请”；她从来不先说“请”。“你看着呢。{o}是怎么做到的？”
# en: A practice ring after a bout, a winner being clapped on the back, a proud student standing alone at the edge, very still.
scene [c11f7d] = 练习场上一局刚结束，赢家正被人拍着后背，一个骄傲的学生独自站在场边，一动不动。
# en: Tell her what you saw
opt.left.label [68bb2b] = 告诉她你看到了什么
# en: You walk her through it: {o}'s feint, the half-step back, the moment she overreached. Lyra listens without blinking. "Again," she says to herself, and goes to the ring, and doesn't come to supper.
opt.left.say.1 [649c24] = 你给她一步步讲：{o}的佯攻，半步后撤，她冒进的那一刻。莱拉听着，眼都不眨。“再来，”她对自己说，转身去了练习场，晚饭也没来吃。
# en: "Ask {o}."
opt.right.label [15b1e3] = “去问{o}。”
# en: Lyra looks at you as if you've suggested she eat soup with a fork. Then she goes and asks. You watch {o}, startled, show her the feint, and Lyra, stiffly, shows {o} something back.
opt.right.say.1 [b7874f] = 莱拉看着你，像你建议她用叉子喝汤。然后她真的去问了。你看着吃了一惊的{o}给她演示那个佯攻，而莱拉僵硬地也教了{o}一招作为回礼。
# en: "I don't ask," Lyra says, and leaves. She doesn't come to supper, and the next morning the practice dummies have scorch marks that weren't there before.
opt.right.say.2 [f6cb57] = “我不问人，”莱拉说着走了。她没来吃晚饭，第二天早上，练习用的假人身上多了几道之前没有的焦痕。

@event kael_between_kindness
# en: He Keeps Leaving
title [765f0c] = 他总是走开
# en: {~{o} has been trying to make friends with Kael for weeks. Every time {o} sits down, Kael finds somewhere else to be.|{o} saved Kael a seat at supper. Kael looked at it as if it might be a trap, and ate standing up.|{o} gave Kael a scarf. Kael said "why?" and meant it, and {o} didn't know what to say.} "What am I doing wrong?" {o} asks you.
text [14dbc5] = {~{o}想跟凯尔交朋友已经好几个星期了。每次{o}一坐下，凯尔就找到别的地方要去。|{o}晚饭时给凯尔留了个位子。凯尔看着那个位子，像在看一个陷阱，然后站着吃完了饭。|{o}送了凯尔一条围巾。凯尔问“为什么？”，是真心在问，{o}不知道该怎么回答。}“我哪里做错了？”{o}问你。
# en: A student holding out a mug of something hot towards a boy with frost on his sleeves, who is already half turned away.
scene [a72fb8] = 一个学生捧着一杯热饮递向袖子上结着霜的男孩，男孩已经转过去一半了。
# en: Tell {o} to give him time
opt.left.label [c0c058] = 告诉{o}给他点时间
# en: {~"He isn't used to it," you say. "Keep sitting down." {o} does. In the third week, Kael stays.|"Kindness makes him nervous," you say. {o} looks at you oddly, and then keeps being kind, quietly, until it doesn't.|"Don't ask why," you say. "Just do it again." The scarf turns up round Kael's neck a month later. Nobody mentions it.}
opt.left.say.1 [1b9435] = {~“他不习惯这个，”你说，“继续坐下就好。”{o}照做了。第三个星期，凯尔留了下来。|“善意会让他紧张，”你说。{o}奇怪地看了你一眼，然后继续默默地对他好，直到他不再紧张。|“别问为什么，”你说，“再来一次就好。”一个月后，那条围巾出现在凯尔的脖子上。没人提起。}
# en: Bring them both to the boathouse
opt.right.label [38e6fe] = 带他们俩去船屋
# en: {~You bring {o} down to the boathouse, where Kael goes in the evenings. Nobody talks much. {o} learns that this is how Kael says yes.|You take the three of you down to the water. Kael shows {o} how to skip a stone, without a word. That is apparently a friendship now.|At the boathouse, Kael is all elbows and silence for an hour. Then he tells {o} the name for snow that falls upward. It is the most you've ever heard him say.}
opt.right.say.1 [a91e71] = {~你带{o}去了船屋，凯尔傍晚常在那儿。没人说多少话。{o}明白了，这就是凯尔说“好”的方式。|你们三个去了水边。凯尔一言不发地教{o}打水漂。这显然就算是交上朋友了。|在船屋里，凯尔手足无措、沉默了一个小时。然后他告诉{o}，那种往上飘的雪叫什么名字。这是你听他说过最多的话。}

@event kael_between_steps_in
# en: Frost on the Floor
title [cd99fb] = 地上的霜
# en: Some older students have {o} pinned against the corridor wall over something about a borrowed book, and it is turning ugly. Before you can move, the air goes cold enough to sting. Kael is standing at the end of the corridor, very still, and frost is feathering up the walls around him.
text [1207bf] = 几个高年级生为了一本借来的书，把{o}堵在走廊墙边，事情越闹越难看。你还没来得及动，空气就冷得刺人。凯尔站在走廊尽头，一动不动，霜花正沿着他四周的墙壁向上蔓延。
# en: A corridor with frost feathering up the walls around one still student, a group of others backing away from a cornered classmate.
scene [3bc59d] = 走廊里，霜花正沿着墙壁围着一个一动不动的学生向上蔓延，一群人从被逼到墙角的同学身边往后退。
# en: Back him up
opt.left.label [e6a7f9] = 站到他身边
# en: You step up beside him. The older students look at the walls, at Kael's face, at you, and decide the book wasn't worth it. Kael walks {o} to the infirmary without a word. Later, he asks you, very seriously, whether he did it right.
opt.left.say.1 [8b0fd0] = 你走到他身旁。那几个高年级生看看墙壁，看看凯尔的脸，又看看你，决定那本书不值得。凯尔一言不发地陪{o}去了医务室。后来，他非常认真地问你，他这么做对不对。
# en: Fetch a prefect instead
opt.right.label [cd8621] = 去找级长
# en: You run for a prefect. By the time you're back the corridor is empty and the walls are dripping, and Kael is gone. {o} tells you he didn't do anything; he just stood there until they left. He doesn't speak of it. He avoids you, a little, for a few days.
opt.right.say.1 [d82535] = 你跑去找级长。等你回来，走廊里空无一人，墙上在滴水，凯尔也走了。{o}告诉你，他什么都没做，只是站在那儿，直到那些人离开。他绝口不提这件事。之后几天，他有点躲着你。

@event bram_between_writes_up
# en: Name in the Ledger
title [a261df] = 名字上了记录簿
# en: {~Bram has {o} by the sleeve for "loitering with intent", which turns out to mean waiting for you.|Bram is writing {o} up for "an insolent hat". {o}'s hat is a perfectly ordinary hat.|Bram has caught {o} running on the stairs, and is reading out the rule number with relish.} {o} looks at you over Bram's shoulder: help.
text [460a2d] = {~布拉姆揪着{o}的袖子，罪名是“意图不轨地逗留”，其实就是在等你。|布拉姆正在给{o}记一笔，罪名是“无礼的帽子”。{o}的帽子是顶再普通不过的帽子。|布拉姆抓到{o}在楼梯上跑，正津津有味地念着校规编号。}{o}越过布拉姆的肩膀看着你：救命。
# en: A prefect with a red sash writing in a ledger while a student argues, a third student hurrying over.
scene [802cba] = 一个披着红色绶带的级长正在记录簿上写字，一个学生在争辩，第三个学生匆匆赶来。
# en: Plead {o}'s case
opt.left.label [f1b202] = 替{o}求情
# en: {~"Rule fourteen is about loitering with intent," you say. "{o} had no intent. Look at {o.them}." Bram looks. He crosses it out, with ill grace.|You argue that a hat cannot be insolent. Bram argues that it can. You win on a technicality he invented himself last term. He hates that.|You remind Bram that he ran on the same stairs on Tuesday. He goes red, says "prefect's business", and lets {o} go.}
opt.left.say.1 [80779e] = {~“第十四条说的是意图不轨地逗留，”你说，“{o}没有意图。你看看{o.them}。”布拉姆看了看。他不情不愿地划掉了。|你论证帽子不可能无礼。布拉姆论证可以。你凭着一条他自己上学期发明的细则赢了。他恨死了。|你提醒布拉姆，他星期二也在这段楼梯上跑过。他脸一红，说了句“级长公务”，放{o}走了。}
# en: {~"And a demerit for you, for obstruction." Bram writes it with a flourish. {o} mouths "sorry" at you.|Bram writes up {o}, then you, then {o} again for laughing. It's a productive afternoon for the ledger.|"Noted," says Bram, and writes up {o} anyway, and adds a little note in the margin about you.}
opt.left.say.2 [30190c] = {~“你也记一笔，妨碍公务。”布拉姆大笔一挥。{o}冲你做口型：“对不起。”|布拉姆给{o}记了一笔，又给你记了一笔，然后因为{o}笑了又记了一笔。记录簿度过了一个充实的下午。|“已记录，”布拉姆说，照样给{o}记了一笔，还在页边给你添了条小注。}
# en: Take the demerit for {o}
opt.right.label [1920b3] = 替{o}领下这次处分
# en: {~"Write me up instead. It was my fault." Bram looks at you for a long moment and writes your name. Afterwards, gruffly, he says, "That was decent." Then he walks off before you can answer.|You say {o} was waiting for you, so it's your demerit. Bram, baffled, agrees. {o} buys you a cake.|You take it. Bram writes it slowly. You catch him, much later, crossing it out when he thinks nobody's looking.}
opt.right.say.1 [b48d5d] = {~“记我吧。是我的错。”布拉姆看了你好一会儿，写下了你的名字。事后他粗声粗气地说：“这事做得体面。”没等你回答就走了。|你说{o}是在等你，所以处分该是你的。布拉姆一头雾水地同意了。{o}请你吃了块蛋糕。|你领了。布拉姆写得很慢。很久以后，你撞见他趁没人注意时把它划掉了。}

@event bram_between_prank
# en: The Sash
title [83b6ff] = 绶带
# en: {o} has a pot of dye, a plan and a grudge. Bram's prefect sash hangs on its peg outside the bathhouse every evening at eight. "Pink," says {o}, glowing. "Just for one day. Are you in?"
text [a4d36d] = {o}有一罐染料、一个计划和一肚子怨气。每晚八点，布拉姆的级长绶带都挂在浴室外的挂钩上。“粉色，”{o}容光焕发，“就一天。你加入吗？”
# en: Two students crouched behind a pillar with a pot of dye, a prefect's red sash hanging on a peg nearby.
scene [b18be1] = 两个学生拿着一罐染料蹲在柱子后面，附近的挂钩上挂着一条级长的红色绶带。
# en: Be the lookout
opt.left.label [d31cde] = 负责望风
# en: Bram wears a pink sash to breakfast before he notices. The refectory goes very quiet, and then very loud. He knows it was {o}. He suspects you. He never proves it.
opt.left.say.1 [36277f] = 布拉姆戴着粉色绶带去吃早饭，走进去才发现。膳堂先是一片寂静，然后炸开了锅。他知道是{o}干的。他怀疑你。他从来没能证明。
# en: Bram comes out of the bathhouse early, and finds you standing very innocently next to his sash and a pot of pink dye. The demerits take him most of a page.
opt.left.say.2 [fbf4eb] = 布拉姆提早从浴室出来，发现你正一脸无辜地站在他的绶带和一罐粉色染料旁边。他写处分写了大半页。
# en: Talk {o} out of it
opt.right.label [4aa154] = 劝{o}打消念头
# en: "It's his whole world, that sash," you say. "It wouldn't be funny to him. It would be the end of the world." {o} looks at you oddly, and puts the dye away. Bram never finds out how close it was.
opt.right.say.1 [f2c778] = “那条绶带就是他的一切，”你说，“对他来说那不好笑。那是天塌了。”{o}奇怪地看了你一眼，把染料收了起来。布拉姆始终不知道那次有多险。

@event bram_between_coaching
# en: Prefect's Business
title [869dc4] = 级长公务
# en: You go into the duelling hall late and find Bram there, without his sash, patiently correcting {o}'s footwork. {o} is terrible. Bram is being kind about it. They both freeze when they see you. "Prefect's business," says Bram, too quickly.
text [98f565] = 你深夜走进决斗厅，发现布拉姆在那儿，没戴绶带，正耐心地纠正{o}的步法。{o}练得糟透了。布拉姆却很和气。看见你，两人都僵住了。“级长公务，”布拉姆说得太快了。
# en: A duelling floor late at night, a prefect patiently correcting a younger student's stance, both freezing as a third student opens the door.
scene [e221a8] = 深夜的决斗场上，一个级长正耐心地纠正低年级学生的站姿，第三个学生推开门时两人都愣住了。
# en: Tease him about it
opt.left.label [8849ef] = 取笑他
# en: "Prefect's business," you repeat, delighted. Bram goes the colour of his sash. He's short with you for a week, and keeps coaching {o} anyway, which you suspect was never in question.
opt.left.say.1 [950837] = “级长公务，”你乐不可支地重复了一遍。布拉姆的脸红得跟他的绶带一个颜色。接下来一个星期他对你都没好气，可照样继续教{o}——你怀疑这从来就不是问题。
# en: Say you never saw a thing
opt.right.label [173993] = 说你什么也没看见
# en: You back out of the door. The next morning Bram passes you in the corridor and says, without looking at you, "Don't make it weird." You don't. {o} wins a practice bout the following week, and Bram claps once, loudly, then stops.
opt.right.say.1 [468532] = 你退出了门外。第二天早上，布拉姆在走廊里与你擦肩而过，眼睛都没看你，说了句：“别搞得怪怪的。”你没有。下个星期{o}赢了一场练习赛，布拉姆响亮地拍了一下手，然后停了。

@event corvin_between_odds
# en: Corvin Makes a Book
title [dbd12d] = 科尔文开了盘
# en: {o} and {p} are going to settle it with wands in the courtyard at sunset, and Corvin is making a book. "Seven to four on {o}, saint," he says, chalking it on the back of a door. "Want in? It's practically charity. I'm charity."
text [11f52f] = {o}和{p}打算日落时在庭院里用魔杖了结恩怨，科尔文正在开盘。“{o}，七赔四，圣人，”他边说边用粉笔写在门背后，“要不要来一注？这简直是做慈善。我就是慈善。”
# en: A student with a deck of cards tucked behind one ear writing odds in chalk on the back of a door, a small crowd pressing coins into his hand.
scene [b0e215] = 一个耳后夹着一副牌的学生正用粉笔在门背后写赔率，一小群人往他手里塞硬币。
# en: Put a crown on {o}
opt.left.label [9bc252] = 押一克朗在{o}身上
# en: {o} wins in a flash of green sparks, and Corvin pays you out with a flourish and a wince. "Beginner's luck. I'll get it back. I always get it back."
opt.left.say.1 [270fe5] = {o}在一阵绿色火花中赢了，科尔文潇洒又肉疼地付了钱。“新手运气。我会赢回来的。我总能赢回来。”
# en: {p} wins, with a hex nobody saw coming. Corvin pockets your crown with real sympathy. "Should've asked me," he says. "I'd have told you. For a fee."
opt.left.say.2 [f0d948] = {p}赢了，用了一道谁都没料到的咒语。科尔文真诚同情地收起了你那枚克朗。“早该问我的，”他说，“我会告诉你的。收费的。”
# en: Tip off a prefect
opt.right.label [4c63af] = 向级长告密
# en: The prefects break it up before the first spell, and confiscate the chalk. Corvin is one detention from being sent home, and he knows exactly who told. He doesn't say anything. That's worse than if he had.
opt.right.say.1 [af5682] = 级长们在第一道咒语之前就把事情平息了，还没收了粉笔。科尔文再挨一次禁闭就要被送回家，而他很清楚是谁告的密。他什么都没说。这比他说了更糟。

@event corvin_between_debt
# en: Corvin Owes {o}
title [ac4c6b] = 科尔文欠{o}的钱
# en: Corvin owes {o} eight crowns, and has owed it since the leaves turned. {o} has an IOU in Corvin's handwriting, with a small drawing of a goat on it. {o} would like you, as Corvin's friend, to collect.
text [e795b7] = 科尔文欠{o}八克朗，从叶子变黄时欠到现在。{o}手里有一张科尔文亲笔写的欠条，上面还画了只小山羊。{o}希望你，作为科尔文的朋友，去把钱要回来。
# en: A student waving a scrap of paper at another, who is shrugging with both hands empty and grinning.
scene [697341] = 一个学生朝另一个挥着一张纸条，对方咧嘴笑着，摊开两只空手耸了耸肩。
# en: Pay it yourself
opt.left.label [3d512f] = 自己替他还
# en: You pay {o} and tell Corvin he owes you now. "Saint," he says, appalled and touched in equal measure. "Who does that?" He pays you back three weeks later, in coins and a very good story about where he got them.
opt.left.say.1 [62eb17] = 你付了钱给{o}，然后告诉科尔文，他现在欠你了。“圣人，”他又惊恐又感动，“谁会这么干？”三个星期后他还了你，用的是硬币，外加一个关于钱从哪儿来的好故事。
# en: Get Corvin to pay
opt.right.label [1ae443] = 让科尔文自己还
# en: You corner Corvin and refuse to laugh at any of his jokes until he pays. It takes four jokes. He pays {o}, all eight, and draws {o} a better goat as interest.
opt.right.say.1 [fc652e] = 你把科尔文堵住，在他还钱之前对他的任何笑话都不笑。这花了四个笑话。他把八克朗全还给了{o}，还给{o}画了只更好的山羊当利息。
# en: Corvin turns it into a joke, then a card trick, then a story about trolls, and by the end you've somehow agreed it's {o}'s fault for lending. {o} doesn't find that funny.
opt.right.say.2 [84af7c] = 科尔文把事情变成一个笑话，又变成一个牌技，又变成一个关于巨魔的故事，到最后你不知怎么竟同意这是{o}自己借钱的错。{o}一点都不觉得好笑。

@event corvin_between_witness
# en: Where Corvin Was
title [5d18c8] = 科尔文当时在哪儿
# en: {o} is up before the headmistress: a silver inkstand gone from the library, and {o} was seen near it. Corvin knows {o} didn't take it; he saw who did, at two in the morning. To say so, he'd have to say where he was at two in the morning. "One more detention, saint," he says quietly. "You know what that means."
text [9d3599] = {o}被叫到了院长面前：图书馆丢了一个银墨水台，有人看见{o}在附近。科尔文知道不是{o}拿的；凌晨两点，他看见了是谁拿的。可要说出来，他就得说出自己凌晨两点在哪儿。“再一次禁闭，圣人，”他低声说，“你知道那意味着什么。”
# en: A student in a dark stairwell holding up an unlocked padlock, another student beside him shaking their head urgently.
scene [cd4a0d] = 昏暗的楼梯间里，一个学生举着一把被打开的挂锁，旁边另一个学生拼命摇头。
# en: Tell him to speak up
opt.left.label [87da40] = 劝他说出来
# en: Corvin goes in, and tells it straight, without a single joke. The headmistress gives him a long look and a warning, not a detention, "in view of the circumstances". {o} doesn't know what to say. Corvin says it for both of them: "Don't make a habit of being innocent near me."
opt.left.say.1 [489e7a] = 科尔文进去了，一个笑话都没讲，把事情原原本本说了。院长看了他很久，“鉴于情况特殊”，只给了警告，没给禁闭。{o}不知道该说什么。科尔文替两人都说了：“别养成在我附近当无辜者的习惯。”
# en: Corvin shakes his head. "I can't, saint. I can't go home." You don't push. {o} gets the detention, and the real thief is never named, and Corvin can't look at {o} for weeks.
opt.left.say.2 [d1e1f0] = 科尔文摇摇头。“我做不到，圣人。我不能回家。”你没有再逼他。{o}挨了禁闭，真正的小偷始终没被点名，好几个星期科尔文都不敢看{o}。
# en: Find another way to clear {o}
opt.right.label [de66a3] = 另想办法替{o}洗清
# en: You go through the library ledger until midnight and find that the inkstand was booked out for cleaning to someone else entirely. {o} is cleared. Corvin buys you a drink and doesn't say why.
opt.right.say.1 [e05e7c] = 你把图书馆的登记簿翻到半夜，发现那个墨水台被另一个人借去清洗了。{o}洗清了嫌疑。科尔文请你喝了一杯，没说为什么。
# en: You turn the library inside out and find nothing anyone will believe. {o} serves the detention. Corvin sits with {o} at supper every night of it.
opt.right.say.2 [6fa756] = 你把图书馆翻了个底朝天，却找不到任何能让人信服的东西。{o}挨了禁闭。禁闭的每个晚上，科尔文都陪{o}吃晚饭。

@event nessa_between_story
# en: The Human Angle
title [9164ce] = 人情味
# en: {o} failed a practical exam badly enough that the lecturer wrote home, and somehow Nessa has heard. "It's a story about pressure," she says, in headline voice. "The human angle. I'd change the name. Mostly." {o} has found out, and caught you in the corridor first. "Please. She'll listen to you."
text [b3e8b9] = {o}的一场实践考试考砸了，砸到讲师写信寄回了家，而内莎不知怎么听说了。“这是一个关于压力的故事，”她用标题腔说，“人情味。我会改掉名字。大部分吧。”{o}知道了，先在走廊里拦住了你。“求你了。她会听你的。”
# en: A newspaper office cluttered with proofs, an editor holding up a draft headline while a student in the doorway begs her not to run it.
scene [86f2ec] = 堆满校样的报社办公室里，一位编辑举着一张标题草稿，门口的学生正求她别登。
# en: Talk Nessa out of it
opt.left.label [f2d423] = 劝内莎打消念头
# en: You put it to her plainly: it's not a story about pressure, it's a story about {o}. Nessa goes very quiet, the way she does off the record. Then she spikes it. "You're right. I hate that you're right."
opt.left.say.1 [d71347] = 你直截了当地告诉她：这不是一个关于压力的故事，是一个关于{o}的故事。内莎安静了下来，就像她不公开记录时那样。然后她撤了稿。“你说得对。我讨厌你说得对。”
# en: "Everyone's a story," Nessa says. "Some just aren't finished." She runs it, with the name changed. Everyone knows who it is. {o} doesn't speak to either of you for a fortnight.
opt.left.say.2 [bf9eb0] = “人人都是一个故事，”内莎说，“只是有些还没写完。”她登了，改了名字。可人人都知道是谁。{o}两个星期没跟你们俩说话。
# en: Offer her a better story
opt.right.label [f7aa4c] = 给她一个更好的故事
# en: You give Nessa something of your own instead: a long, unflattering account of your worst week this term. She takes it, delighted. {o}'s story never runs. Yours does, on page two, and people are very kind about it for a week.
opt.right.say.1 [c23d11] = 你转而给了内莎一个你自己的故事：一篇冗长又不太体面的叙述，讲你本学期最糟糕的一个星期。她如获至宝。{o}的故事始终没登。你的登在了第二版，接下来一个星期，大家都对你特别和气。

@event nessa_between_match
# en: Match of the Month
title [d38ac6] = 本月佳偶
# en: The Lumen Ledger is launching "Match of the Month", anonymous and entirely scientific, and Nessa needs a first nomination by the printers' deadline. She has heard you know {o}. "Who's {o} sweet on? You don't have to say. Just write it down. That's not saying."
text [01170c] = 《流明纪事报》要推出“本月佳偶”栏目，匿名，绝对科学，内莎需要在付印截止前拿到第一个提名。她听说你认识{o}。“{o}暗恋谁？你不用说出来。写下来就行。写下来不算说。”
# en: An editor at a cluttered desk holding out a quill and a blank form titled "Match of the Month", grinning.
scene [04dbc8] = 一位编辑坐在乱糟糟的书桌后，笑着递出一支羽毛笔和一张标题为“本月佳偶”的空白表格。
# en: Nominate {o}
opt.left.label [216a97] = 提名{o}
# en: You write a name down. On Friday the whole castle reads that "a certain student in the year" is pining for "a certain other student", with details. {o} recognises every detail. So does the other student, it turns out, and the next week they're seen at the Gilded Newt together. {o} is still furious with you.
opt.left.say.1 [c0e567] = 你写下了一个名字。星期五，全城堡都读到“本年级的某位同学”正苦苦思慕“另一位同学”，还附有细节。{o}认出了每一个细节。结果另一位同学也认出来了，下个星期，有人看见他们一起去了镀金蝾螈酒馆。{o}至今还在生你的气。
# en: Tell Nessa it's not yours to print
opt.right.label [c9fb2c] = 告诉内莎这轮不到你来登
# en: "Off the record?" says Nessa. "It's off the record that I'm not telling you," you say. She laughs, and nominates herself instead, which sells out the issue.
opt.right.say.1 [9c750a] = “不公开记录？”内莎说。“不公开记录的是，我不告诉你，”你说。她笑了，转而提名了她自己，那一期卖了个精光。

@event mir_between_owl
# en: The Owl Has Opinions
title [282081] = 猫头鹰有意见
# en: Mir's clockwork owl, which remembers deadlines, birthdays and, slightly, grudges, has taken against {o}. It hoots when {o} comes in. It drops screws on {o} from the rafters. "It's not personal!" says Mir. "Probably. It might be personal. I didn't build it to be personal."
text [9b2d8f] = 米尔的发条猫头鹰会记住截止日期、生日，还有，稍微记一点仇——它看{o}不顺眼。{o}一进门它就叫。它从房梁上往{o}身上扔螺丝。“这不是针对谁！”米尔说，“大概吧。也可能是针对的。我造它的时候没打算让它针对谁。”
# en: A clockwork owl perched on a workshop lamp, glaring with brass eyes at a student who is ducking, while its maker apologises with both hands.
scene [5180da] = 一只发条猫头鹰蹲在工坊的灯上，用黄铜眼睛瞪着一个正在躲闪的学生，它的制造者举着双手道歉。
# en: Help Mir find out why
opt.left.label [bfbdef] = 帮米尔找出原因
# en: You go through the owl's memory spool with Mir, half the night, and find it: {o} once moved a teacup off the owl's favourite shelf, in the first week. Mir has a long, gentle talk with the owl. The screws stop. Mostly.
opt.left.say.1 [ebbbf3] = 你和米尔翻查了猫头鹰的记忆发条，翻了半个晚上，终于找到了：第一周时，{o}把一只茶杯从猫头鹰最喜欢的架子上挪开过。米尔和猫头鹰进行了一次漫长而温和的谈话。螺丝不再掉了。基本上。
# en: You and Mir take the owl apart and put it back together and it is still furious with {o}. "It's a feature now," Mir decides. {o} starts wearing a hat.
opt.left.say.2 [b29ea3] = 你和米尔把猫头鹰拆开又装好，它还是对{o}怒气冲冲。“现在这是个功能了，”米尔宣布。{o}开始戴帽子了。
# en: Tell {o} to apologise to it
opt.right.label [6bc3a5] = 让{o}去给它道歉
# en: You suggest {o} apologise. {o} stands under the rafters and apologises to the owl, formally, for whatever it was. The owl considers this for a whole minute, then hoots once, and from then on drops screws on {o} only on Tuesdays. Mir is moved almost to tears.
opt.right.say.1 [d5a6bb] = 你建议{o}去道个歉。{o}站在房梁下，郑重其事地向猫头鹰道歉，不管当初做错了什么。猫头鹰考虑了整整一分钟，叫了一声，从此只在星期二往{o}身上扔螺丝。米尔感动得差点哭了。

@event mir_between_blunt
# en: Probably Fine
title [47432a] = 大概没问题
# en: {~{o} asked to help Mir in the workshop. Mir said, cheerfully, "No, you'll touch things," and then talked to a gearbox for ten minutes.|{o} showed Mir a design. Mir said, "That'll explode," with total delight, and went back to the lathe.|{o} has been holding the same lamp for Mir for an hour. Mir has thanked the lamp twice and {o} not once.} {o} finds you afterwards. "Do they even like me?"
text [cd845b] = {~{o}想在工坊里给米尔帮忙。米尔开开心心地说：“不行，你会乱碰东西的。”然后对着一个齿轮箱说了十分钟话。|{o}给米尔看了一张设计图。米尔兴高采烈地说：“这会爆炸的，”然后回到了车床边。|{o}给米尔举着同一盏灯举了一个小时。米尔谢了那盏灯两次，一次都没谢{o}。}事后{o}来找你。“TA到底喜不喜欢我？”
# en: A workshop bench strewn with gears, an artificer talking excitedly to a half-built machine while a classmate stands to one side, looking hurt.
scene [11288c] = 摆满齿轮的工坊长凳边，一位工匠兴奋地对着半成品机器说话，一个同学站在一旁，神情受伤。
# en: Translate for Mir
opt.left.label [c5f106] = 替米尔翻译
# en: {~You explain that "you'll touch things" is high praise from Mir; it means you'd be interested. {o} goes back. Mir gives {o} a screwdriver of {o.their} very own, which is practically a ring.|"It'll explode" means "I'd want to watch," you tell {o}. {o} brings the design back, and Mir spends three hours making it explode properly.|You tell {o} that Mir thanks lamps because lamps can't be hurt. {o} laughs. The next time, Mir, prompted by you, thanks {o}, and then the lamp, in that order.}
opt.left.say.1 [c134ab] = {~你解释说，“你会乱碰东西”在米尔那儿是极高的赞誉，意思是你会感兴趣。{o}回去了。米尔送了{o}一把专属的螺丝刀，这几乎等于一枚戒指。|你告诉{o}，“这会爆炸的”意思是“我想看看”。{o}把设计图拿了回去，米尔花了三个小时让它好好地炸了一回。|你告诉{o}，米尔谢灯是因为灯不会受伤。{o}笑了。下一次，在你的提醒下，米尔先谢了{o}，再谢了灯，按这个顺序。}
# en: Tell Mir directly
opt.right.label [c596c4] = 直接告诉米尔
# en: {~"Oh!" says Mir, stricken. "Oh no. Probably I should say things to people." They go and say several things to {o}, all at once, most of them about gears. It works.|Mir listens, goggles pushed up, and then goes and apologises to {o} with a small clockwork frog. The frog says sorry. Mir says it too.|Mir takes it very seriously and writes "SAY THANK YOU TO {o}" on the workshop wall in chalk, where it stays for a year.}
opt.right.say.1 [6dfedf] = {~“哦！”米尔大惊失色，“哦不。我大概应该对人说点什么。”TA跑去一口气对{o}说了好几件事，大部分是关于齿轮的。管用了。|米尔把护目镜推到额头上听完，然后带着一只小小的发条青蛙去向{o}道歉。青蛙说了对不起。米尔也说了。|米尔非常认真，用粉笔在工坊墙上写下“要对{o}说谢谢”，那行字在墙上留了一年。}
# en: {~Mir doesn't really hear it; they're halfway into a gearbox. "Hm? Yes. Probably," they say. {o} gives up on the workshop.|"But I do like {o}," says Mir, baffled, "I let {o} hold the lamp." You don't get further than that.|Mir nods along and then forgets, which is very Mir. {o} decides the workshop isn't for {o.them}.}
opt.right.say.2 [b7bcc3] = {~米尔其实没听进去；TA的半个身子在齿轮箱里。“嗯？是。大概吧，”TA说。{o}放弃了工坊。|“可我是喜欢{o}的啊，”米尔困惑地说，“我都让{o}举灯了。”谈话到此为止。|米尔连连点头，然后就忘了，很米尔。{o}认定工坊不适合{o.them}。}
